--- everything else

no easy markdown preview in helix editor.

no easy default setup -> had to look up how to set cpp version, look up diff between clang and gcc++. mismatch between lsp version and gcc version configured. pretty bad. had to look up project configuration from my old, unrelated project for compiler flags. pretty bad DX. easy desync between .clangd vs CPP_FLAGS in makefile. not great DX either.

documentation, particularly build step easily can and will mismatch the project build setup in makefile. easy desync.

should this language be for good devs or for people with skill issues? maybe just 4myself

it is not obvious to me why the entrypoint to the program is called "main". is there a side program? other ideas: begin. start. init. entrypoint. entry. launch. initiate. main. say.

todo-like function in the language itself. finding not implemented edge cases can be hard in jira tickets / elsewhere.

--- peak c++ observations

Peak reflection, unconsting the const.
```cpp
	const string entry_point_path = "./delight-language-program/start";
	std::string& mutable_ref = const_cast<std::string&>(entry_point_path);
	mutable_ref = "new/path";  // Now you can modify it
```

explicit errors. e.g. if you have (int / int), the division operation, one int can be 0. user should be explicitly informed about such edge case. that's very important

the problem with todos in general as part of syntax that syntax has limitations and cannot be called everywhere. oh man.

would be great if language was vertical-heavy by design, e.g.:
some_variable_name        = 
some_variable_name_longer = 
